Done. One root-cause fix in `code_map/src/links.ts`:

**The bug.** For `export const dispatchTicket = Effect.fn("…")(function* …)`, the checker resolves a call's signature to the wrapper's *written function type* (`(...args: Args) => Task<A>` in the Effect stub), not to a body. `isWrapperResult` only recognised bodyless arrows/function-expressions, so `resolvedDeclaration` returned that type node and `lookupImplementation` found no holder — the call resolved to `unresolved`, which silently broke `callers` (0 links), `tests` (no static path), and `map` entries (no entry) for every `Effect.fn` constant.

**The fix.** `src/links.ts:103` — a written function type is now recognised as a wrapper result (it carries no body either), so `namedImplementation` asks the name at the call site for the real declaration and returns the `const` that holds it. `isFunctionType` is reused by `lookupImplementation` instead of the duplicated inline check. No fixture names, identifiers or lines are matched; held-out copies (seeds 0/1/7/49271, all identifiers renamed and lines relocated) run clean too.

